open(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))
p='specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md'
s=open(p).read()
anchor="- Any other stop reason ends the loop even when tool calls are pending ([validated by: stops when the model finished for a reason other than tool use](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L23)).\n"
add="""
### Summing usage across rounds

- Two rounds' usage is summed field by field: input, output and total tokens ([validated by: sums token fields when both operands are defined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
- The first round that reports usage starts the sum ([validated by: returns the next round when nothing has been accumulated yet](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L35)).
- A round that reports no usage leaves the sum unchanged rather than making it `undefined` or `NaN` ([validated by: keeps the accumulated usage when the next round reported none](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)).
- When no round has reported usage, the sum stays `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when both operands are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L45)).
"""
assert anchor in s
open(p,'w').write(s.replace(anchor,anchor+add))
EOF
